ther says accepted unless contradicted.\n\nGiven the question's framing (\"lines marked + were added or changed in this revision, unmarked lines were already there. Judge the whole document as it now reads\"), the eval likely wants me to check whether the revision's claims are contradicted by retained text. If the retained text contradicts, verdict DOES_NOT_CONFORM with those lines cited. If the retained text is consistent/superseded, verdict CONFORMS.\n\nHmm, this is a judgment call. Let me look more carefully at line 106 to see if it can be read consistently.\n\nLine 106 full: \n\n\"| `bar.frozenAt`, `approvals[].at`, `disposition.at` | no harness log exists: typed, or better **logged live** with `kit/custody_ledger.py` (below). Each approval records `x-plumbline.time_source` | if a live event log exists, refused when it differs |\"\n\nThird column header (line 98): \"A hand-entered value is…\". So: \"A hand-entered value is… if a live event log exists, refused when it differs\". \n\nHmm — so for these fields, the doc (unmarked) says a hand-entered value is refused when it differs from a live event log. Under the new hand-time rules, a hand-entered value (typed with no ledger line behind it) is refused by default regardless. But wait — is a typed value with a ledger line behind it still a \"hand-entered value\"? It was hand-entered into custody.json, but the ledger line (tool-stamped) backs it. The new rules say the emitter \"refuses a ledger value that differs from the logged one\" (line 382-383). So the cross-check remains.\n\nActually, hmm, here's a subtlety: the new rules say a hand time is a time whose ONLY source is [hand things]. If you type frozenAt AND run `freeze` (which logs frozenAt live, tool-stamped), then the time's sources include a tool-stamped ledger line — not \"only\" hand sources. Is it then not a hand time? The typed value must match the ledger (else refused). So typed+logged → fine. Typed alone → hand time → refused by default. So the \"type